    <string name="colortools_film_intro">Spectral simulation of analog film: the image exposes a negative that is developed and printed on paper (slide film is scanned directly), with grain, halation and diffusion. Put it last in the node chain – it turns the image into a finished display image.</string>
    <string name="colortools_film_mode_full">Whole film</string>
    <string name="colortools_film_mode_effects">Effects only</string>
    <string name="colortools_film_mode_effects_hint">Only halation, diffusion, grain, glare and sharpness – the image keeps its own colors, contrast and encoding, so the node can go anywhere in the chain.</string>
